    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "360c9675_fc327503",
        "filename": "finder/finder.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 762,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-31T22:37:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What would you do to make it simpler? It seems to me that bundling \u003cdone\u003e into workResponse makes it easy to determine at a glance that there won\u0027t be any concurrency misorderings involving receiving \u003cdone\u003e too early, whereas if there are multiple channels, then the reader has to check the way that the channels interact to determine whether there can be ordering issues.",
      "parentUuid": "aec6fa81_2f88c48d",
      "revId": "95fb00e63d8fb419928115fa1b4490681e21b913",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b280ecc_a298e710",
        "filename": "finder/finder.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 762,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-31T22:51:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you use unbuffered channels then ordering issues are straightforward, because the other side of the channels are all processed synchronously in the same goroutine.  The writer writes the data before writing done, and the reader sees the data before seeing done.",
      "parentUuid": "360c9675_fc327503",
      "revId": "95fb00e63d8fb419928115fa1b4490681e21b913",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
